{
  "name": "Sensor Level Meter with 7-Segment Digit",
  "description": "A complete sensor-to-digit instrument: a slow 0→5V sensor sweep feeds a 2-bit FLASH ADC (1.25/2.50/3.75V reference ladder + 3 comparators), gate logic converts the thermometer code to binary and decodes it to a 7-segment LED display. As the level rises and falls, the displayed digit steps 0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 2 → 1 → 0, every phase showing the exact standard segment pattern (~7.9mA per lit segment). The full analog→digital→display chain in one circuit. (ngspice-validated across all 7 phases.)",
  "tags": [
    "sensor",
    "display",
    "led",
    "7-segment",
    "adc",
    "flash-adc",
    "mixed-signal",
    "flagship"
  ],
